Lab 20: Final Project: Manage Multicluster Environment with RHACM
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Set up and configure Red Hat Advanced Cluster Management (RHACM) for multicluster management
Deploy and manage applications across multiple OpenShift clusters
Implement comprehensive security policies across clusters
Configure observability and monitoring for multicluster environments
Troubleshoot common multicluster management issues
Apply best practices for enterprise-scale multicluster operations
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of Kubernetes and OpenShift concepts
Familiarity with YAML configuration files
Experience with command-line interface operations
Knowledge of container orchestration principles
Understanding of networking concepts in containerized environments
Completion of previous RHACM labs or equivalent experience
Lab Environment Setup
Ready-to-Use Cloud Machines: Al Nafi provides pre-configured Linux-based cloud machines with all necessary tools installed. Simply click Start Lab to begin - no need to build your own virtual machines or install software.

