Task 1: Set Up RHACM for Multicluster Management
Subtask 1.1: Verify RHACM Installation and Access
First, let's verify that RHACM is properly installed and accessible on your hub cluster.

Access the hub cluster:
# Switch to the hub cluster context
oc config use-context hub-cluster

# Verify cluster connection
oc whoami --show-server
Check RHACM installation status:
# Verify RHACM operator installation
oc get operators -A | grep advanced-cluster-management

# Check RHACM pods status
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management
Access RHACM web console:
# Get RHACM console URL
oc get route multicloud-console -n open-cluster-management -o jsonpath='{.spec.host}'

# Get admin credentials
oc whoami -t
Subtask 1.2: Configure Hub Cluster Settings
Configure the hub cluster with optimal settings for multicluster management.

Create namespace for multicluster resources:
# Create dedicated namespace
oc create namespace multicluster-demo

# Set as default namespace
oc config set-context --current --namespace=multicluster-demo
Configure cluster resource quotas:
# Create file: cluster-resource-quota.yaml
cat << EOF > cluster-resource-quota.yaml
apiVersion: v1
kind: ResourceQuota
metadata:
  name: multicluster-quota
  namespace: multicluster-demo
spec:
  hard:
    requests.cpu: "10"
    requests.memory: 20Gi
    limits.cpu: "20"
    limits.memory: 40Gi
    persistentvolumeclaims: "10"
EOF

# Apply the quota
oc apply -f cluster-resource-quota.yaml
Verify hub cluster readiness:
# Check cluster status
oc get managedclusters

# Verify RHACM components
oc get pods -n open-cluster-management-hub
Subtask 1.3: Import and Configure Managed Clusters
Import the two managed clusters into RHACM for centralized management.

Import cluster-east:
# Create managed cluster resource
cat << EOF > managed-cluster-east.yaml
apiVersion: cluster.open-cluster-management.io/v1
kind: ManagedCluster
metadata:
  name: cluster-east
  labels:
    environment: production
    region: east
    vendor: OpenShift
spec:
  hubAcceptsClient: true
EOF

# Apply the managed cluster
oc apply -f managed-cluster-east.yaml
Generate import command for cluster-east:
# Get the import command
oc get secret cluster-east-import -n cluster-east -o jsonpath='{.data.import\.yaml}' | base64 --decode > cluster-east-import.yaml

# Display the import command
echo "Run this command on cluster-east:"
echo "oc apply -f cluster-east-import.yaml"
Import cluster-west:
